{%- comment -%}
  Curated customer reviews (Trust).
  Renders ONLY when the merchant has entered real reviews as blocks in the
  Theme Editor — no blocks, no section. Never write reviews or fabricate a
  star count. These are the store's own reviews, hand-entered — no link to
  an external review profile, no embedded third-party widget, no scraped
  content. `source_note` is an optional caption ONLY (plain text, never a
  link) kept for the PDP instance of this same section
  (templates/product.json); leave it blank on the homepage instance.

  Layout: left column is the static trust anchor — heading + aggregate
  rating from settings.rating_value / settings.rating_count (global,
  shop-wide — the same numbers used wherever a rating is shown elsewhere,
  never invented here). Right column cycles through the review blocks.

  The cycle is CSS-only, on purpose: it must not depend on theme.js and
  must degrade honestly. All blocks are
  stacked in one CSS-grid cell (`grid-area: 1 / 1`, so the container's height
  is always the tallest card, no JS measuring) and each gets the same
  @keyframes with a negative animation-delay of its own index × dwell time —
  the classic delay-offset crossfade, computed once here from the real block
  count so N reviews always divide the loop evenly (no dead gap, no double
  showing). prefers-reduced-motion cancels the animation in home-extras.css
  and falls back to a plain stacked list — nothing here reads that media
  query in JS, the browser just never plays the @keyframes.

  Accessibility note: cards that are mid-fade are hidden with opacity only,
  not visibility/aria-hidden, so a screen reader still reaches every quote in
  document order regardless of which one is visually on top — the audio
  experience is effectively always the reduced-motion list.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign count = section.blocks.size
  assign rv = settings.rating_value | times: 1.0
  assign filled = rv | round
-%}
{%- if count > 0 -%}
<section class="sec--tight tp" id="pdp-reviews" aria-label="{{ 'reviews.aria' | t }}">
  <div class="wrap tp__grid">
    <div class="tp__intro reveal">
      {%- liquid
        comment
          The merchant's heading wins in every language (Translate & Adapt
          localizes section settings); 'reviews.heading' is the fallback for a
          blank one only. Reassigning on every secondary locale discarded it.
        endcomment
        assign tp_heading = section.settings.heading
        if tp_heading == blank
          assign tp_heading = 'reviews.heading' | t
        endif
      -%}
      <h2 class="dl">{{ tp_heading | escape }}</h2>
      {%- if settings.rating_value != blank -%}
        <div class="tp__rating">
          {%- capture rating_label -%}{{ 'product.rating.aria_short' | t: value: settings.rating_value }}{%- endcapture -%}
          {%- render 'stars', value: settings.rating_value, size: 18, label: rating_label -%}
          <p class="stmt-sm mute">{{ settings.rating_value }}{% if settings.rating_count != blank %} · {{ settings.rating_count }} {{ 'product.rating.reviews_label' | t }}{% endif %}</p>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.settings.source_note != blank -%}
        <p class="stmt-sm mute">{{ section.settings.source_note | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
    {%- comment -%} ALL REVIEWS AT ONCE, SWIPEABLE.

    This used to stack every card in ONE grid cell and cross-fade between them on
    a 5-second timer. So a shopper saw a single quote, had no idea three more
    existed, could not go back to one that had passed, and on a 467px-tall block
    that was one quote for a lot of page. Trust copy that hides itself is not
    doing its job.

    Now they are a scroll-snapped row: swipe on a phone, two-and-a-bit visible on
    desktop, and the count is obvious from the peeking next card. Native
    scrolling only — no JS, no timer, keyboard and screen readers get a plain
    horizontally scrollable list with every quote in document order. {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="tp__cards reveal" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-label="{{ count }} customer reviews, scroll for more">
      {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
        {%- liquid
          comment
            A review the merchant entered wins in every language — these are
            real customer words, so a locale default must never overwrite one.
            The per-index keys (reviews.rN_quote / rN_meta) only fill a field
            left empty, with a translation-missing guard, exactly like the FAQ
            blocks. Quote and meta resolve independently. Names stay as entered.
          endcomment
          assign tp_quote = block.settings.quote
          assign tp_meta = block.settings.meta
          if tp_quote == blank
            assign tp_qk = 'reviews.r' | append: forloop.index | append: '_quote'
            assign tp_qt = tp_qk | t
            unless tp_qt contains 'Translation missing' or tp_qt contains 'translation missing'
              assign tp_quote = tp_qt
            endunless
          endif
          if tp_meta == blank
            assign tp_mk = 'reviews.r' | append: forloop.index | append: '_meta'
            assign tp_mt = tp_mk | t
            unless tp_mt contains 'Translation missing' or tp_mt contains 'translation missing'
              assign tp_meta = tp_mt
            endunless
          endif
        -%}
        <figure class="tp__card" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
          {%- comment -%} Reviews and the UGC selfie band share one card
          format — customer photo on top of each card, quote under it. The
          meta line (country · date) is not rendered.

          NO PHOTO, NO <img>. This used to fall back to a
          social-proof-<position>.webp theme asset that the theme has never
          shipped, guarded only by an onerror that hides the element after the
          request has already failed. The section ships with three review
          blocks and no images, so EVERY fresh install fired three hard 404s
          and reserved 338px of empty box per card before the handler ran. A
          review is its stars and its words; the photograph is the optional
          part, and an unset one is simply absent. {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if block.settings.image != blank -%}
            <img class="tp__card-photo"
              src="{{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 480, height: 640, crop: 'center' }}"
              srcset="{{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 480, height: 640, crop: 'center' }} 480w, {{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 720, height: 960, crop: 'center' }} 720w"
              sizes="(max-width: 720px) 74vw, 340px"
              width="480" height="640" loading="lazy" alt="">
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- capture card_label -%}{{ block.settings.stars }} out of 5 stars{%- endcapture -%}
          {%- render 'stars', value: block.settings.stars, size: 15, label: card_label -%}
          <blockquote class="tp__card-quote stmt">{{ tp_quote | escape }}</blockquote>
          {%- comment -%} Meta line format: "<country> · <recent date>". {%- endcomment -%}
          <figcaption class="tp__card-by">
            <span class="lbl">{{ block.settings.name | escape }}</span>
            {%- if tp_meta != blank -%}<span class="stmt-sm mute">{{ tp_meta | escape }}</span>{%- endif -%}
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Customer reviews",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Trusted by thousands" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "source_note", "label": "Source note (optional)", "info": "Plain caption only, e.g. a date range. NEVER name a review platform here: these reviews are entered by hand and the aggregate figure is a shop setting, so crediting an external review service claims a verification that did not happen. Leave empty to hide." }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "review",
      "name": "Review",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "range", "id": "stars", "label": "Stars", "min": 1, "max": 5, "step": 1, "default": 5 },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "quote", "label": "Review text", "info": "Paste the real review verbatim — never write reviews yourself." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "name", "label": "Reviewer name" },
        { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Photo", "info": "Optional. Leave empty for a quote-only card." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "meta", "label": "Meta line (not rendered)", "info": "Kept for data safety; the card no longer prints it." }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Customer reviews" }]
}
{% endschema %}
